cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "RAVEN: Receiver-conditioned Action-Value ENcoding for Finite-Symbol Multi-Agent Communication"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/sswun/RAVEN"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-28
authors:
  - family-names: Sun
    given-names: Shuwei
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-4809-8557"
abstract: >-
  RAVEN is a communication method for cooperative multi-agent reinforcement
  learning with a finite alphabet (four symbols, two bits per message) and a
  one-step message delay. A sender's symbol is chosen so that, inside the
  receiver's own decision context, the receiver's centred action-value profile
  matches the profile it would have with the sender's full information. The
  objective is solved offline by exact codebook construction from a
  centralised teacher, or online by aligning a deployed symbol branch with a
  continuous reference branch in a value-decomposition learner.
keywords:
  - multi-agent reinforcement learning
  - emergent communication
  - discrete communication
  - value decomposition
  - bandwidth-limited communication
